{
  "id": "05-ballast",
  "name": "Ballast",
  "format_version": 1,
  "seed": 1005,

  // Teaches: mass adds up. One blob is not heavy enough for the plate, so
  // both go in the trough, and the door does not latch so neither can be
  // taken out again. The trough is shallow — a step down, not a trap — and
  // the blobs sit proud of it, so crossing means walking over the ballast
  // you just laid.
  //
  // The second blob starts in the trough with the door still shut. That
  // is the level explaining itself: the player sees weight on the plate
  // and a door that has not opened, which asks the question the level
  // answers, instead of making them discover it by failing.
  //
  // Two earlier drafts are worth recording, because both were geometry
  // problems wearing a puzzle's clothes. A version with two pits and a
  // plate in each made the player drag the second blob across the first
  // pit, over a gap they cannot stand on while holding something. A
  // version with the plate flat on the open floor let the player shove the
  // blobs straight off it on the way past.

